  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="228"/>
    <location value="139"/>
    <location value="234"/>
    9.3.1.8. Admixtures
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="18"/>
    <location value="244"/>
    <location value="444"/>
    <location value="257"/>
<![CDATA[Admixtures shall conform to ASTM C260 / C260M , 'Air - Entraining Admixtures for Concrete', or ASTM C494 / C494M, 'Chemical Admixtures for Concrete', as applicable. r5]]>    
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="269"/>
    <location value="222"/>
    <location value="275"/>
    9.3.1.9. Cold Weather Requirements
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="285"/>
    <location value="258"/>
    <location value="291"/>
    When the air temperature is below 5 ° C , concrete shall be,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="293"/>
    <location value="389"/>
    <location value="299"/>
    (a) kept at a temperature of not less than 10 ° C or more than 25 ° C while being mixed and placed, and
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="301"/>
    <location value="301"/>
    <location value="307"/>
    (b) maintained at a temperature of not less than 10 ° C for 72 h after placing.
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(2)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="317"/>
    <location value="320"/>
    <location value="322"/>
    No frozen material or ice shall be used in concrete described in Sentence (1).
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="334"/>
    <location value="245"/>
    <location value="342"/>
