  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="73"/>
    <location value="339"/>
    <location value="79"/>
    9.4.4.6. Walls Supporting Drained Earth (See Appendix A.)
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="90"/>
    <location value="458"/>
    <location value="95"/>
    Except where constructed in accordance with Section 9.15., walls supporting drained earth shall be designed,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="97"/>
    <location value="482"/>
    <location value="110"/>
    (a) for a pressure equivalent to that exerted by a fluid with a density of not less than 480 kg/m 3 and a depth equal to that of the retained earth, or
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="112"/>
    <location value="445"/>
    <location value="118"/>
    (b) in accordance with Section 4.2. so as to be able to resist the loads and effects described in Article 4.1.2.1.
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(2)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="127"/>
    <location value="293"/>
    <location value="133"/>
    Walls supporting other than drained earth shall be designed,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="135"/>
    <location value="377"/>
    <location value="140"/>
    (a) for the pressure described in Clause (1)(a) plus the fluid pressure of the surcharge, or
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="142"/>
    <location value="445"/>
    <location value="148"/>
    (b) in accordance with Section 4.2. so as to be able to resist the loads and effects described in Article 4.1.2.1.
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="169"/>
