    Notes to Table 9.7.3.3.:
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="15"/>
    <location value="292"/>
    <location value="453"/>
    <location value="308"/>
    <content><![CDATA[ U-values for specific products can be determined according to measures referenced in AAMA/WDMA/CSA 101/I.S.2/A440, North American Fenestration Standard/Specification for Windows, Doors, and Skylights'.  Temperature index (I) is determined r11.1]]></content>
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="43"/>
    <location value="302"/>
    <location value="449"/>
    <location value="322"/>
<![CDATA['NAFS - accordin g to the physical test procedure given in CSA A440.2/A440.3, 'Fenestration Energy Performance/User Guide to CSA A440.2 - 14, Fenestration Energy Performance'.]]>    
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(2)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="326"/>
    <location value="366"/>
    <location value="332"/>
    <content> There is no appropriate test procedure available for testing the condensation resistance of sloped glazing.</content>
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(3)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="15"/>
    <location value="335"/>
    <location value="435"/>
    <location value="348"/>
    <content><![CDATA[ Where the U-value in this Table differs from the U-value provided in MMA Supplementary Standard SB10, 'Energy Efficiency Requirements' or MMA Supplementary Standard SB - 12, 'Energy Efficiency for Housing', the most restrictive U -value shall apply. r6]]></content>
