  </table>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="404"/>
    <location value="268"/>
    <location value="410"/>
    9.9.7.4. Number and Spacing of Egress Doors
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="420"/>
    <location value="317"/>
    <location value="426"/>
    Except for dwelling units , at least two egress doors shall be provided where,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="428"/>
    <location value="418"/>
    <location value="441"/>
    (a) the area of a room or suite exceeds 200 m² in a Group D, E, F2 and F3 occupancy , or 150 m² in a Group C occupancy , or
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="443"/>
    <location value="401"/>
    <location value="448"/>
    (b) the distance measured from any point within a room or suite to the nearest egress door exceeds 25 m.
  </list>
  <page_footer>
    <layer value="furniture"/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="483"/>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="489"/>
    48
  </page_footer>
  <page_footer>
    <layer value="furniture"/>
