  <page_header>
    <layer value="furniture"/>
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="22"/>
    <location value="83"/>
    <location value="28"/>
    9.10.6.2.
  </page_header>
  <page_header>
    <layer value="furniture"/>
    <location value="160"/>
    <location value="22"/>
    <location value="347"/>
    <location value="28"/>
    2012 Building Code Compendium
  </page_header>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="55"/>
    <location value="219"/>
    <location value="61"/>
    9.10.6.2.  Heavy Timber Construction
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="71"/>
    <location value="433"/>
    <location value="84"/>
    Heavy timber construction shall be considered to have a 45 min fire-resistance rating when it is constructed in accordance with the requirements for heavy timber construction in Article 3.1.4.7.
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="96"/>
    <location value="171"/>
    <location value="103"/>
    9.10.7.  Steel Members
  </heading>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="116"/>
    <location value="279"/>
    <location value="122"/>
    9.10.7.1.  Protection of Structural Steel Members
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="133"/>
    <location value="420"/>
    <location value="146"/>
    Except as provided in Article 3.2.2.3., structural steel members used in construction required to have a fireresistance rating shall be protected to provide the required fire-resistance rating .
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="18"/>
    <location value="157"/>
    <location value="441"/>
    <location value="177"/>
    9.10.8.  Fire-Resistance, Combustibility and Sprinklers in Relation to Occupancy, Height and Supported Elements r1
  </heading>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="189"/>
    <location value="306"/>
    <location value="195"/>
    9.10.8.1.  Fire-Resistance Ratings for Floors and Roofs
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="206"/>
    <location value="434"/>
    <location value="219"/>
    Except as otherwise provided in this Subsection, the fire-resistance ratings of floors and roofs shall conform to Table 9.10.8.1.
  </list>
  <table>
    <location value="29"/>
    <location value="257"/>
    <location value="452"/>
    <location value="320"/>
    <caption>
      <location value="136"/>
      <location value="228"/>
      <location value="348"/>
      <location value="249"/>
      Table 9.10.8.1. Fire Resistance Ratings for Structural Members and Assemblies Forming Part of Sentence 9.10.8.1.(1)
    </caption>
