    9.20.2.7.
  </page_header>
  <picture>
    <location value="59"/>
    <location value="10"/>
    <location value="122"/>
    <location value="27"/>
  </picture>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="55"/>
    <location value="197"/>
    <location value="62"/>
    9.20.2.  Masonry Units
  </heading>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="75"/>
    <location value="232"/>
    <location value="81"/>
    9.20.2.1.  Masonry Unit Standards
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="92"/>
    <location value="205"/>
    <location value="97"/>
    Masonry units shall comply with,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="99"/>
    <location value="285"/>
    <location value="105"/>
<![CDATA[(a) ASTM C73, 'Calcium Silicate Brick (Sand - Lime Brick)',]]>    
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="107"/>
    <location value="431"/>
    <location value="112"/>
<![CDATA[(b) ASTM C126, 'Ceramic Glazed Structural Clay Facing Tile, Facing Brick, and Solid Masonry Units',]]>    
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="114"/>
    <location value="239"/>
    <location value="119"/>
<![CDATA[(c) ASTM C212, 'Structural Clay Facing Tile',]]>    
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="45"/>
    <location value="121"/>
    <location value="308"/>
    <location value="127"/>
<![CDATA[(d) CAN/CSAA82 'Fire Masonry Brick Made from Clay or Shale', r11.1]]>    
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="45"/>
    <location value="128"/>
    <location value="251"/>
    <location value="134"/>
<![CDATA[(e) CSA A165.1, 'Concrete Block Masonry Units', r11.1]]>    
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="45"/>
    <location value="135"/>
    <location value="259"/>
    <location value="142"/>
<![CDATA[(f) CSA A165.2, 'Concrete Brick Masonry Units', or r11.1]]>    
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="45"/>
    <location value="143"/>
    <location value="261"/>
    <location value="149"/>
<![CDATA[(g) CSA A165.3, 'Prefaced Concrete Masonry Units'. r11.1]]>    
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="161"/>
    <location value="167"/>
    <location value="167"/>
    9.20.2.2.  Used Brick
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="177"/>
    <location value="449"/>
    <location value="183"/>
    Used bricks shall be free of old mortar, soot or other surface coating and shall conform to Article 9.20.2.1.
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="194"/>
    <location value="177"/>
    <location value="200"/>
    9.20.2.3.  Glass Blocks
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="211"/>
    <location value="425"/>
    <location value="217"/>
    Glass blocks shall not be used as loadbearing units or in the construction of fireplaces or chimneys .
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="228"/>
    <location value="199"/>
    <location value="234"/>
    9.20.2.4.  Cellular Concrete
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="245"/>
    <location value="444"/>
    <location value="250"/>
    Masonry made with cellular concrete shall not be used in contact with the soil or exposed to the weather.
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="262"/>
    <location value="141"/>
    <location value="268"/>
    9.20.2.5.  Stone
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="278"/>
    <location value="205"/>
    <location value="284"/>
    Stone shall be sound and durable.
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="295"/>
    <location value="311"/>
    <location value="301"/>
    9.20.2.6.  Concrete Units Exposed to the Weather
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="45"/>
    <location value="311"/>
    <location value="458"/>
    <location value="325"/>
<![CDATA[Concrete blocks exposed to the weather shall have weight and water absorption characteristics conforming to Classes A, B, C or D, described in CSA A165.1, 'Concrete Block Masonry Units'. r11.1]]>    
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="336"/>
    <location value="223"/>
    <location value="342"/>
    9.20.2.7.  Compressive Strength
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="353"/>
    <location value="351"/>
    <location value="358"/>
    The compressive strength of concrete blocks shall conform to Table 9.20.2.7.
  </list>
  <table>
    <location value="60"/>
