  <heading level="2">
    <location value="33"/>
    <location value="405"/>
    <location value="120"/>
    <location value="410"/>
    Notes to Table 9.20.5.2.C.:
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="33"/>
    <location value="413"/>
    <location value="433"/>
    <location value="418"/>
    <content> These spans assume that the beam supports the veneer, a wood stud wall and a maximum specified roof live load of 2.3 kN/m.</content>
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(2)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="33"/>
    <location value="420"/>
    <location value="305"/>
    <location value="426"/>
    <content> Where the steel beam carries floor loads or larger roof loads, refer to Article 9.23.4.3.</content>
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(3)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="33"/>
    <location value="427"/>
    <location value="99"/>
    <location value="433"/>
    <content> See Appendix A.</content>
  </list>
