  <heading level="2">
    <location value="63"/>
    <location value="295"/>
    <location value="143"/>
    <location value="301"/>
    Notes to Table 9.26.3.1.:
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="63"/>
    <location value="303"/>
    <location value="160"/>
    <location value="309"/>
    <content> See Sentence 9.26.3.1.(2).</content>
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(2)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="63"/>
    <location value="310"/>
    <location value="160"/>
    <location value="316"/>
    <content> See Sentence 9.26.3.1.(3).</content>
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="328"/>
    <location value="261"/>
    <location value="335"/>
    9.26.4.  Flashing at Intersections
  </heading>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="45"/>
    <location value="348"/>
    <location value="356"/>
    <location value="354"/>
    9.26.4.1.  Required Flashing at Intersections (See Appendix A.) r11.1
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="364"/>
    <location value="469"/>
    <location value="377"/>
    Except where the omission will not adversely affect adjacent supported or supporting elements, flashing shall be installed at junctions between roofs and,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="379"/>
    <location value="206"/>
    <location value="385"/>
    (a) walls that rise above the roof, and
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="387"/>
    <location value="318"/>
    <location value="392"/>
    (b) guards that are connected to the roof by other than pickets or posts.
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="60"/>
    <location value="404"/>
    <location value="158"/>
    <location value="410"/>
    9.26.4.2.  Materials
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="420"/>
    <location value="259"/>
    <location value="426"/>
    Sheet metal flashing shall consist of not less than,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="428"/>
    <location value="178"/>
    <location value="433"/>
    (a) 1.73 mm thick sheet lead,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="435"/>
    <location value="199"/>
    <location value="441"/>
    (b) 0.33 mm thick galvanized steel,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="443"/>
    <location value="168"/>
    <location value="448"/>
    (c) 0.33 mm thick copper,
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="450"/>
    <location value="168"/>
    <location value="456"/>
    (d) 0.35 mm thick zinc, or
    <ldiv/>
    <location value="72"/>
    <location value="457"/>
    <location value="179"/>
    <location value="463"/>
    (e) 0.48 mm thick aluminum.
  </list>
  <page_footer>
    <layer value="furniture"/>
    <location value="234"/>
    <location value="483"/>
    <location value="310"/>
    <location value="489"/>
    Division B - Part 9
  </page_footer>
  <page_footer>
    <layer value="furniture"/>
    <location value="468"/>
    <location value="483"/>
    <location value="484"/>
    <location value="489"/>
    179
  </page_footer>
