  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="388"/>
    <location value="176"/>
    <location value="395"/>
    9.27.5.5.  Fastener Materials
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="405"/>
    <location value="441"/>
    <location value="418"/>
    Nails or staples for the attachment of cladding and wood trim shall be corrosion-resistant and shall be compatible with the cladding material.
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="30"/>
    <location value="430"/>
    <location value="217"/>
    <location value="436"/>
    9.27.5.6.  Expansion and Contraction
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="42"/>
    <location value="446"/>
    <location value="427"/>
    <location value="452"/>
    Fasteners for metal or vinyl cladding shall be positioned to permit expansion and contraction of the cladding.
  </list>
