  <heading level="2">
    <location value="32"/>
    <location value="358"/>
    <location value="101"/>
    <location value="364"/>
    Notes to Table A-12:
  </heading>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(1)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="32"/>
    <location value="366"/>
    <location value="451"/>
    <location value="387"/>
    Beam and lintel spans are calculated based on a maximum supported length of 4.9 m.  Spans may be increased by 5% for supported lengths of not more than 4.3 m, by 10% for supported lengths of not more than 3.7 m, and by 25% for supported lengths of not more than 2.4 m.
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(2)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="32"/>
    <location value="389"/>
    <location value="450"/>
    <location value="409"/>
    For ridge beams, supported length means half the sum of the rafter, joist or truss spans on both sides of the beam.  For lintels, supported length means half the sum of truss, roof joist or rafter spans supported by the lintel plus the length of the overhang beyond the lintel.
    <ldiv>
      <marker>(3)</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="32"/>
    <location value="410"/>
    <location value="184"/>
    <location value="417"/>
    Provide a minimum bearing length of 76 mm.
  </list>
